{"name":"Boredom Buster","hex":"#ff8e51","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"boredom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being bored. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","An instance or period of being bored; a bored state."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boredom"},{"term":"buster","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone who or something that bursts, breaks, or destroys a specified thing.","Forming compounds denoting a team, weapon, or device specialized in the destruction of the first element."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buster"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boredom","blocks":[{"text":"In conventional usage, boredom, ennui, or tedium is an emotion characterized by uninterest in one's surrounding, often caused by a lack of distractions or occupations. However, boredom is not well defined. It is distinct from depression and apathy. Boredom may damage mental health, but it also seems to have improved creativity in humans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Souvenir_Seller_-_Moscow_-_Russia_cropped.JPG/330px-Souvenir_Seller_-_Moscow_-_Russia_cropped.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boredom","wikidata":"Q34255"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/La_Touche_Lennui_1893.jpg/500px-La_Touche_Lennui_1893.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/La_Touche_Lennui_1893.jpg/500px-La_Touche_Lennui_1893.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boredom by Gaston de La Touche, 1893","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALa_Touche_Lennui_1893.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Bored_girl.jpg/500px-Bored_girl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_